Face.; Facies.

@AC 18. See <Deep-Abyssus>.

@19[end]. These Knowledges are here called "the faces of the waters."

@32[end]. Inmost things are signified by the face.

@173. Two faces were as it were induced on me... When the Angels perceive that their faces are received, they know that the man is dead. @SE 1097.

@222. "The face of Jehovah" (Genesis 3:8) = mercy, peace, and all good. Illustrated. @358[end]. @387. @3195[end].

@355. "His faces fell" (Genesis 4:5) = that the interiors were changed. @358. @359.

@358. With the ancients, the face = internal things, because internal things shine forth through the face. In ancient times their faces agreed exactly with their internals...

@--. When charity shone from the face, they said that the face was elevated; but when the contrary, they said that the face fell.

