@3587. To "go out from the faces" (Genesis 27:30) = when these things ceased; thus when the state was changed.

@3631. The Societies which constitute the province of the face... @4800.

@--. They were allowed to effigy a face in various ways by influx.

@3741[2]. From the affections of the animus, which present themselves to view in the face...

@3804[2]. In human faces, in which for the most part the affections effigy themselves, no two are exactly alike. @6232[3]. @7236[2].

@3901[5]. Under <Eagle>, see this reference.

@3934[3]. That the face is the image of the animus...

