@--[11]. Therefore, also, "the face of Jehovah" = the interior things of the Church, of the Word, and of worship. Illustrated.

@--[22]. But "the face," when predicated of man, = the animus and his affection, thus the interiors which belong to his mind. Explained, Illustrated.

@--[35]. References to passages on the subject of the face.

@455[10]. "The faces of Jehovah" = the good of love.

@463. To "fall upon the faces" = humiliation of heart, because it corresponds to this humiliation. @688, Explained.

@659[2]. "The faces of Jehovah" = the things which are revealed in the Word.

@684[29]. "His faces" = the Divine love, and enlightenment thence.

@730[39]. "Face to face" = to the life, and to the acknowledgement.

@811[6]. To "cover the face that he see not the earth" (Ezekiel 12:12) = that the truths of good are no longer seen in the Church. @1145[8].

