@4096[2]. Does not fall into the understanding. @9543.

@5492[end]. It falls into this when it descends.

@6567. "They fell before him" (Genesis 50:18) = submission.

@6876[end]. The idea falls into nothing.

@8831. "And many of them fall" (Exodus 19:21) that thus they would perish.

@9086. To "fall" = to perish. (See <Donkey>.)

@--. To "fall" also = to make a slip by mistake.

@10184[6]. To "descend (from the housetop)" (Luke 17:31) = a relapse to the former state.

@10492. To "fall" or be slain (Exodus 32:28) = to be closed... Evils and falsities are what close the internal man...

@HH 302[2]. He would at once fall down dead. @TCR 118.

