@DLW 5. In order that this may fall into the understanding...

@202[3]. The thoughts of the Angels do not fall into natural ideas.

@DP 277. a. Where the tree falls, there it lies. @SE 2805. @DMin 4645, Explained @4646.

@AR 333. To "fall from heaven into the earth" (Revelation 6:13) = to disappear. ( = to perish. @AE 402.)

@339. To "fall upon them, and hide them" (Revelation 6:16) = to protect against the influx from Heaven; and as this is done by confirmations of evil by falsity, and of falsity from evil, these are signified.

@370. To "fall upon the faces and adore" (Revelation 7:11) = humiliation of heart, and adoration thence. Explained. @AE 463.

@408. "There fell from heaven a great star..." (Revelation 8:10) = the appearance of Own intelligence... @409. @AE 517. @518, Explained.

@515. "The tenth part of the city fell" (Revelation 11:13)... To "fall" = to sink down into Hell. ( = to disappear. @AE 675.)

@521. To "fall upon their faces..." (Revelation 11:16) = the highest adoration... @AE 688.

@631. "Babylon is fallen, is fallen..." (Revelation 14:8)... To "fall" = to be dispersed... ( = to be damned and utterly destroyed. @AE 879.)

@712. "The cities of the nations fell" (Revelation 16:19)... Fall Away To "fall" = to be destroyed. ( = to be dissipated. @AE 1020.)

@755. Under <Babel>, see this reference.

@AE 77. "I fell at His feet" (Revelation 1:17) = adoration from humiliation.

@388[14]. To "fall" (Ezekiel 39:4) = to perish.

@391[26]. To "fall" (Ezekiel 6:13) = to be damned.

@AE 481. "Neither shall the sun fall upon them..." (Revelation 7:16) = that they shall not have evil from concupiscences.

@518. To "fall" (when said of the stars) = to perish.

@535[2]. Illustrated.

@644[24]. This man yields in temptations, and falls into grievous falsities, which are the falsities of evil; and therefore it is said, "great was the fall of it" (Matthew 7:27).

@1004[5]. Therefore, when an Angel merely thinks of it, he falls from Heaven.

@1097. "Is fallen, is fallen" (Revelation 18:2) = destruction and ruin, thus the Last Judgment... for they are then cast into Hell.

