@6044[2]. He grieved intensely, wanting to receive truths, and thus reject falsities; but could not; because while falsities and the evils thence are in the mind, truths cannot enter...

@AE 107. The things which man apprehends from himself... are falsities...

@131[2]. Falsities cannot be cast out except by combats from these truths. Signified.

@--[5]. They who are in falsities there, cannot endure truth. Signified.

@--[17]. That those who believe falsities will perish by falsities. Signified.

@138. When he comes into spiritual temptation, he is among those Spirits who are in falsities... @164.

@166. Under <Son>, see this reference.

@177. The total dispersion of falsities. Signified.

@235[2]. From false principles nothing but falsities follow... @237[8].

