@474. Falsities, being opposite to truths... must first be removed...

@--[2]. They who will come into Heaven are vastated as to falsities.

@478. They who are in falsities from ignorance, and still in the good of life according to their religion, cannot be saved until the falsities with them have been removed... And therefore, when they emerge from the temptations, the falsities still remain, although they have been removed by means of truths... Hence it is that unless those who have been in falsities from ignorance in the world were constantly kept in truths by the Lord, they would relapse into falsities. Signified.

@511[2]. When truths conjoin themselves with affections merely natural, they are... falsities; for affection merely natural falsifies them.

