@--[3]. Falsities do not injure such, because there is no evil in them: falsities from evil are the very falsities which are from Hell...

@889[2]. That dense falsity presses on them, and flows forth from them... (For) man is his own truth or falsity, not only as to the thoughts from his will, but also as to his universal body...

@--[5]. These falsities sometimes appear to the sight as smoke from conflagrations; sometimes as black clouds; sometimes as black and fetid waters; sometimes as foul smells.

@950[2]. (For) the falsities which inundated the Church could only be dispersed by genuine truth opened in the Word...

@1007[2]. With those who are in falsities as to doctrine, but in goods as to life, there is no conjunction of evil and falsity.

@1035[2]. There is no spiritual drunkenness from falsities which are not from evil; for these falsities do not pervert and destroy spiritual truths... falsities -falsitates- not from evil may be compared to waters which are not pure But falsities from evil may be compared to wine or strong drink which induces drunkenness.

@1130. For he who is in the love of evil is also in the love of falsity; for falsity confirms evil.

@LJPost 207. How much principles of falsity injure, and avert the mind from things to be done.

@5M 1. The cupidity within flows into the rationality of the merely Natural, and darkens its light, so that they see nothing but falsities in the place of truths.

@ConvAng 15. A false principle in spiritual things falsifies all things. It falsifies all things of the Word... without man knowing it, while he is reading the Word... This falsity is not manifested, except when it is set in the middle of the view of the thought.

@CanonsNC 24. Redemption. 1. 11. From a single falsity there flow forth falsities in a continuous series, until there is no truth left.

@Inv 16. All theologians, when preaching, know nothing of the falsities of their religion... But let them know that the falsities which they have imbibed in the schools are clinging to them interiorly; and that the other things are simply between their lips; and therefore these falsities ought by all means to be rooted out.

@51. If falsities -falsitates- are confirmed from the Word, they do not ascend into Heaven, but are rejected, and are dispersed on the way with a loud report.

@DeConsum 1. Falsities have to be rooted out before truths are implanted.

