Far off, To be.; Elongare.
Removal to a distance.; Elongatio.

@AC 2685. To be "far off" (Genesis 21:16) = to be absent.

@7457. That they would quite remove themselves. Signified.

@7461. "Not to go far away" (Exodus 8:28) = not to be far off.

@9261. "Thou shalt set thyself far away" (Exodus 23:7) = aversion.

@--. This is from the removals to a distance which appear in the Spiritual World...

@10546. "By removing far from the camp" (Exodus 33:7) = remote from those externals...

