Feasting.; Epulatio.

@HH 359. (Man is allowed to feast, etc.)

@CL 3[3]. Feastings with Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob. @6. @256. Epulus. @AE 617[2].

@DWis 11. 4. He is withheld from the delight of mere feasting...

Feast. Feast, To make a.; Feriari.

@AC 7884. To "make a feast" (Exodus 12:14) = the worship of the Lord. @7882.

@9286. "Three times ye shall make a feast to Me in the year" (Exodus 23:14) = permanent worship of the Lord and thanksgiving on account of deliverance from damnation. To "make a feast" or to hold a feast -festum agere-, = the worship of the Lord from a glad mind on account of deliverance from damnation.

@9296. Occurs. @--[4].

Feast.; Festum.
Festal.; Festalis.

