@6537[end]. The feast of tabernacles = holy worship, thus worship from good and truth.

@7093. "And hold a feast to Me in the wilderness" (Exodus 5:1) = that from a glad mind they may worship the Lord in the obscurity of faith in which they are. To "hold a feast" = worship from a glad mind... because the feast was to be held at "a way of three days" from Egypt, thus in a state of no infestation by falsities: that is, in a state of freedom... Moreover the feasts which were instituted among that people, which were three in the year, are said to have been instituted in memory of deliverance from slavery in Egypt; that is, in a spiritual sense, in memory of deliverance from infestation by falsities by the advent of the Lord into the world. Illustrated. @7882.

@7664. "Because it is a feast of Jehovah to us" (Exodus 10:9) = the worship of the Lord in each and all things.

